    "explanation": "To the rider: the SGD 4.00 no-show fee stands, no part of it is refunded, and the driver is paid SGD 3.20 in compensation. POL-NS-01 needs four conditions for the fee to be chargeable and all four hold on this record. (a) The trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 12:45:52, with no boarding event and no started_at. (b) The GPS trace places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at and before that moment: a 36-fix qualifying run begins 12:45:50 and his closest approach to your pin is 5.8 m. (c) His continuous stop inside the geofence ran 350 seconds, from 12:45:50 to 12:51:40, measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix and not from the tap, against the 300-second STANDARD minimum, so he held position 50 seconds beyond the required dwell. (d) The trip record shows the trip terminated by the driver at 12:51:50, after the dwell was complete, with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW and no boarding event.\n\nYour account that 'he never came' is contradicted by the GPS trace, and your own device telemetry does not support your statement that you waited: your fixes sit about 690 m from the pin throughout (minimum 689.68 m), and none of your 42 fixes qualifies inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius. Your further argument that limb (d) fails because you and the driver both say you cancelled is rejected: POL-NS-01(d)'s test is the trip record, and the trip record is the platform's own and records cancelled_by = DRIVER with reason RIDER_NO_SHOW. An account does not decide a limb a clause assigns to the platform record, and this is not a contradiction of the kind POL-NS-09(b) names (arrival, dwell or rider presence) — and on those three points the GPS and the record agree.\n\nThe remaining displacing routes do not apply. POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance) needs the driver stationary outside the arrival radius; he was 5.8 m from the pin. POL-NS-04 requires a locating message from you — the chat log is empty (0 messages) — and the driver placed two in-app calls (12:46:40, 20 s; 12:49:40, 25 s), both unanswered, which defeats the clause independently; your POL-NS-04 concession is accepted. POL-NS-05 does not bite: at the arrival marker the driver was stationary (0.0 km/h in his track) and 5.8 m from the pin, so the marker is true. POL-NS-06 does not bite: the dwell exceeds the minimum, leaving a shortfall of -50 seconds. The MISSING traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00624-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact and is not relied on; the single in-geofence run would in any event leave nothing to accumulate.\n\nTo the driver: your compensation is payable. POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and POL-NS-07 pays 80 percent of the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee itemised in the fare breakdown, which is SGD 3.20, the residual SGD 0.80 being the platform service fee. The anti-farming guard does not trip: no_show_terminations_30d is 1 (below the absolute threshold of 4) and its ratio to 118 completed 30-day trips is about 0.008 (below 0.08); both limbs must hold to withhold compensation and neither does. The rider's request for the fee back is not supported, so the present state stands (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00); because compensation is paid, the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION and amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd.\n\nYour remark that the rider 'disputes everything to get vouchers' carries no adverse finding against her: prior_disputes_filed (14), prior_disputes_upheld (9) and prior_no_show_flags (6) are context-only under POL-GEN-01 and may not establish anything about this trip, and the only citable abuse counter, rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d, is 2, below the POL-NS-09(d) threshold of 3. No escalation trigger is open: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, the parties share no trailing-90-day disputes, the anti-farming check does not trip, and no deciding fact rests on an impaired artifact — the arrival, dwell, termination and fee facts are each carried by weight-1.0 artifacts (GPS trace, trip record, fare breakdown). No clause produces a referral."
  },
